        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up llapi_fid_test test20",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up llapi_fid_test test20\n\nllapi_fid_test test20 builds a chain of 2000+ nested\ndirectories and calls fid2path on every level.  The cost of\neach call grows with depth, so the loop is quadratic and\naccounts for most of the 200 s CI average of sanity 154g.\n\nCall fid2path on every 100th level, plus the deepest one as\nbefore.  The test still checks the 2000 directory depth.\n\nLocal single-node timings of sanity 154g:\nbefore: 262-358 s (test20 201-279 s)\nafter:  150 s (test20 52 s)\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=154g\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id12d4c42bb7aed02fb529ff41f5224bdd11766d8\n"
      },
